prompt:
On 1 April our platform started to comply with the DCWP minimum-pay rule for food delivery workers ($19.56 per hour on all the time couriers are online, topped up weekly with a true-up where a week falls short), and on the same day the dispatcher started to restrict when couriers can go online to the hours we expect to need them. From 1 July it tightens further: it will grant about 0.49 connected hours per forecast order (0.69 today), and its plan for the payout periods ending in the third quarter is about 6.45 million connected hours in total (the periods ending in the second quarter came to about 7.49 million). Volume is planned flat.

Finance wants to know where the courier money goes in Q3. Based on what you know, the numbers from January to June and that plan, file three forecasts for the third quarter of 2024 (July, August and September together), each with an 80% central prediction interval:

- minimum_pay_true_ups_usd: the sum of the ADJUSTMENTS lines on the COURIER_WEEKLY pay invoices for the payout periods ending in the quarter;
- surge_premium_usd: the surge premium we pay couriers for those same periods, as finance's pay-period report carries it;
- no_courier_cancellations: the number of orders placed in the quarter that we cancel because no courier could be found.

Pay is the sum of base, incentives and adjustments on the weekly courier AP invoices for the periods. Tips are not pay. End date from XX_PAYOUT_PERIODS falling in the month is how we track whether a payout period falls in the month.
